&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scrunch vs. Ahrefs at a&amp;nbsp;Glance&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Choose Scrunch if you want active website optimization for AI crawlers, product-level shopping visibility, or agency pitch workspaces. Choose Ahrefs Brand Radar if you want AI tracking inside an all-in-one SEO platform, backed by a large database of real user search prompts and multi-channel tracking across YouTube, Reddit, and TikTok.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scrunch is an Agent Experience Platform (AXP) from Sitecore. It detects AI agents such as ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity at the edge and serves them a token-light, structured version of your pages, while human visitors see the normal site. Ahrefs Brand Radar tracks AI visibility from inside the Ahrefs ecosystem, so the AI data sits next to Site Explorer, Keywords Explorer, and Rank Tracker.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Quick Scrunch vs. Ahrefs Comparison Table&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scrunch vs. Ahrefs Engine Coverage and Surfaces&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/scrunch-vs-ahrefs-2-20261025-4473636.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Comparison chart of Scrunch and Ahrefs Brand Radar across engine coverage, prompt methodology, actionability, integrations, pricing, and best-fit team."&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An engine is the AI product that generates the answer, such as ChatGPT or Perplexity. A surface is a place where answers or brand mentions appear, such as a Google AI Overview, Google AI Mode, a YouTube video, or a Reddit thread. Comparing the two tools gets easier once you keep those terms separate.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Ahrefs Brand Radar covers 7 platforms on every tier. Scrunch covers 4 LLMs on Core and 9 on Enterprise, with Claude, Gemini, Meta AI, Google AI Mode, and Grok added at the higher tier. If you need broad engine coverage without an enterprise contract, Brand Radar has the edge. Scrunch’s depth shows up elsewhere, in its Shopping module and its bot-side tools. Ahrefs goes wider on surfaces that aren’t LLMs, tracking YouTube transcripts and titles, Reddit, TikTok in beta, and a GBP Monitor for Google Business Profiles.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Which engines matter most for my category?&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Start with the engines your buyers use, then work outward. Your analytics referrals, sales call notes, and customer surveys will show where buyers say they research. Google deserves early attention because of its reach.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Research found that &lt;a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2025/07/22/google-users-are-less-likely-to-click-on-links-when-an-ai-summary-appears-in-the-results/"&gt;18% of Google searches in March 2025 produced an AI summary&lt;/a&gt;, and the rate climbed with longer, question-style searches. If your buyers research with long, conversational queries, Google AI Overviews and AI Mode belong in your first tracking set. Our guide to the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/top-search-engines"&gt;top search engines&lt;/a&gt; can help you map where your audience searches, and the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/evolution-of-search"&gt;evolution of search&lt;/a&gt; gives context on why that mix keeps shifting.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Ecommerce teams should weigh Scrunch’s product-level shopping visibility. Brands with strong video or community footprints should weigh Ahrefs’ YouTube and Reddit tracking.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;How should I validate coverage during a trial?&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scrunch offers a 7-day free trial on entry tiers. Ahrefs doesn’t offer free trials or discounts on Brand Radar, so ask your rep what a pilot looks like. Either way, validate the same way:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ol start="1"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Pick 15 to 25 prompts that mirror real buyer questions, across awareness, comparison, and purchase stages.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Run the same prompts manually in each engine you care about and save the answers.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Compare the tool’s output to your manual results. Check that it reports the same brand mentions and cited sources.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Note any engine you need that the plan doesn’t include.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ol&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Look at how each...

&lt;p&gt;More of your audience now gets answers from AI instead of a list of links. So when someone asks an assistant about your category, the response draws on sources you may never even see, and your brand either shows up in it — or doesn’t.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;That shift changes what &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-in-content-marketing"&gt;AI in content marketing&lt;/a&gt; asks of you. Writing a strong page used to be the finish line. Now you also need to know how AI systems find, select, and cite pages, and that starts with a question many marketers haven’t had a reason to ask yet: what is RAG in AI?&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: The State of AEO in 2026 [Free AI Search Trends Report]" height="79" width="369" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Pew Research Center looked at this behavior in a &lt;a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2025/07/22/google-users-are-less-likely-to-click-on-links-when-an-ai-summary-appears-in-the-results/"&gt;2025 analysis of 900 U.S. adults’ browsing data&lt;/a&gt;. Users clicked a traditional search result on 8% of visits when Google showed an AI summary, compared with 15% of visits without one. Fewer clicks means the answer itself carries more weight, and so do the sources behind it — the pages a system pulls from can shape what it says about you.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide explains RAG in plain language, starting with what it means for your marketing and then covering how it works. You’ll leave with a checklist for making your content easier for retrieval systems to use.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;One caveat up front: retrieval-friendly content can improve machine accessibility, but it doesn’t guarantee retrieval or citation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
