&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is RAG in AI?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;RAG in AI is a method that retrieves relevant information from an external knowledge base before a model generates an answer. The name stands for retrieval-augmented generation, and it also shows up in conversations about GenAI RAG setups. In each case, RAG augments the model’s prompt with retrieved source material, which improves answer grounding.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/what-is-rag-in-ai-1-20261029-8617984.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="what is rag in ai: a method that retrieves relevant information from an external knowledge base before a model generates an answer"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Without RAG, a language model answers from what it absorbed during training. With RAG, it checks a source first. That source can be a help center, a product database, or a set of company documents, and the answer reflects what the model finds there.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why does RAG in AI matter to marketers?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;RAG matters because it connects AI answers to source material, and your content can be that source material.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A standard large language model (LLM) generates answers from patterns it learned during training. That knowledge has a cutoff date and doesn’t include your latest pricing page, product launch, or help article. RAG fills that gap. The system retrieves relevant context from an external knowledge base, then uses it to write the answer.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For marketers, three things follow from that:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your content can be retrieved and cited.&lt;/strong&gt; When an answer engine uses retrieval, the pages it pulls from can influence what it says about your brand.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity and freshness become competitive factors.&lt;/strong&gt; Pages with explicit facts, consistent terminology, and current information give a retrieval system better material to work with.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership matters.&lt;/strong&gt; Someone needs to maintain the source of truth, because a retrieval system can only surface what exists and what it can access.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Answer engines retrieve and cite sources differently, so you can’t predict outcomes for any single platform. What you can do is make your content easier for machines to read, which is the focus of the sections below.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How does RAG in AI work?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;RAG works in three steps: retrieve, augment, generate. If you want the broader picture of what’s happening inside these systems first, our guide on &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/how-does-ai-work"&gt;how AI works&lt;/a&gt; covers the fundamentals.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ol start="1"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retrieve.&lt;/strong&gt; The system takes a question and searches a knowledge base for the most relevant passages.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Augment.&lt;/strong&gt; It adds those passages to the model’s prompt, giving the model source material to work from.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Generate.&lt;/strong&gt; The model writes an answer using both the question and the retrieved material.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ol&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Here’s a marketer-friendly example. Say your company has a help article about resetting a password. Behind the scenes, a RAG system prepares that article in advance:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chunking:&lt;/strong&gt; It splits the article into smaller passages, such as one section per step or topic.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embeddings:&lt;/strong&gt; It converts each chunk into a numerical representation of its meaning, so the system can match by meaning rather than exact keywords.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vector database:&lt;/strong&gt; It stores those embeddings in a database built for fast similarity search.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When someone asks, “How do I reset my password?”, the system finds the closest-matching chunks, adds them to the...

&lt;p&gt;To improve visibility in AI answer engines, content and SEO marketers need to add AEO keywords gap analysis to their strategies. Traditional SEO keyword gaps show which terms a company &lt;em&gt;isn’t&lt;/em&gt; ranking for versus the competition. An AEO keywords gap uses the same principle but with broader criteria, identifying the prompts and questions where a given brand is cited in AI search, but another isn’t.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide offers a practical pathway to find and close the AEO keywords gap, identifying AI citation opportunities a company is missing. It covers how to audit current content and competitor coverage, how to spot high-value gaps to close first, how to turn gaps into answer-ready content that gets cited, and how to track whether it’s working.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-is-an-aeo-keywords-gap"&gt;What is an AEO keywords gap?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#aeo-keywords-gap-vs-traditional-seo-gap"&gt;AEO Keywords Gap vs. Traditional SEO Gap&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-audit-your-aeo-keywords-gap"&gt;How to Audit Your AEO Keywords Gap&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-prioritize-the-right-gaps"&gt;How to Prioritize the Right Gaps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-turn-a-gap-into-answer-ready-content"&gt;How to Turn a Gap Into Answer-Ready Content&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-hubspot-aeo-helps-you-find-and-close-gaps"&gt;How HubSpot AEO Helps You Find and Close Gaps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-measure-progress-over-time"&gt;How to Measure Progress Over Time&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-aeo-keywords-gaps"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About AEO Keywords Gaps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#dont-underestimate-the-value-of-aeo-keyword-gaps"&gt;Don’t underestimate the value of AEO keyword gaps.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is an AEO keywords gap?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An AEO keywords gap is the difference between the questions or topics AI answer engines surface versus the questions a brand answers clearly enough to be cited. The gap refers to keywords, topics, questions, and prompts that a brand hasn’t answered clearly enough to be cited in engines like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The stakes are &lt;em&gt;high&lt;/em&gt; for AEO keyword gaps &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/adapting-to-the-new-era-of-search"&gt;in this new search era&lt;/a&gt;. When a buyer asks an answer engine to recommend a product or solution, rather than a page of links to choose from, they get a paraphrased response or a shortlist directly from AI.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The evidence is in the data: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/company-news/aeo-data-buyers-using-ai-search-more-likely-to-purchase"&gt;HubSpot’s own research&lt;/a&gt; of 3,063 CRM software purchase decision-makers found that &lt;strong&gt;42% of CRM software buyers now use AI search&lt;/strong&gt; as part of their evaluation, and it’s the strongest predictor of purchase intent HubSpot tracks. Referral traffic from AI tools like ChatGPT and Gemini has also tripled over the past year, &lt;a href="https://searchengineland.com/what-13-months-of-data-reveals-about-llm-traffic-growth-and-conversions-470115"&gt;according to Search Engine Land&lt;/a&gt;. If a brand isn’t showing up in the prompts that map to its category, it’s being left off the shortlist before a buyer ever visits a website.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The following bar chart from the Search Engine Land article shows the aggregate referral traffic by month in 2025. Monthly volume climbed steadily throughout the year, with December’s referral traffic roughly three times higher than January’s. The rising traffic reinforces the importance of the AEO keyword gap. More people are searching using AI tools.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/aeo-keywords-gap-1-20261029-9081899.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="Bar chart from Search Engine Land shows the aggregate referral traffic by month in 2025. The rising traffic reinforces the importance of the AEO keyword gap. More people are searching using AI tools."&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Important note:&lt;/strong&gt; An SEO keyword gap and an AEO keywords gap don’t tell the same story, and closing one doesn’t close the other. A page can rank on page one of Google for a term and still never get pulled into an AI-generated answer for that same topic. &lt;a href="https://www.brightedge.com/resources/weekly-ai-search-insights/ai-overviews-one-year-presence-size-citing"&gt;BrightEdge’s analysis of AI Overviews&lt;/a&gt; (AIO) found that only about 17% of sources cited in AIOs also rank in the organic top 10, meaning roughly five out of six AIO citations pull from content that never appears on page one of traditional results.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip: &lt;/strong&gt;While an SEO keyword gap shows where content is missing from rankings, it can’t show where content is ranking well and still getting skipped over in AI-generated answers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;AEO Keywords Gap vs. Traditional SEO Gap&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A traditional keyword gap report answers one question: Which terms does a competitor rank for that a brand doesn’t?&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Gaps between AEO versus SEO are not the same thing. The comparison needs more dimensions than that, because answer engines aren’t just matching keywords. AEO keyword research prioritizes questions, entities, answer formats, and citation potential.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How to Audit Your AEO Keywords Gap&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Auditing an AEO keyword gap is the first step to improving visibility and staying competitive in search. There are four essential steps that make up an AEO keywords gap audit:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;1. Inspect Search Console and SERP patterns.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://search.google.com/u/1/search-console/"&gt;Google Search Console&lt;/a&gt; (GSC) shows which queries are already driving impressions and clicks to a website. While GSC is largely an &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/blog/tabid/6307/bid/22842/4-helpful-tools-for-identifying-the-right-keywords.aspx"&gt;SEO tool with keyword research&lt;/a&gt; capabilities and AEO features in beta, the data is still transferable to AEO (also known as &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/generative-engine-optimization"&gt;GEO&lt;/a&gt;). Queries that are already gaining impressions and clicks are, in theory, associated with your website; the brand already has authority there, which &lt;em&gt;may&lt;/em&gt; transfer to AIO.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Start by exporting data and reviewing keywords in Google Sheets or in an Excel spreadsheet. Look for:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Long-tail queries &lt;/strong&gt;(multiple words in one query). People tend to use more conversational prompts in AI search engines. &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/definit...

&lt;p&gt;Measuring success is a leading challenge for answer engine optimization (AEO) that marketers report today. In &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-aeo"&gt;HubSpot’s State of AEO 2026&lt;/a&gt; report, it was the top challenge among B2B marketers at 23%; among B2C marketers, 26% cited it, behind only understanding how AEO works at 29%.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: The State of AEO in 2026 [Free AI Search Trends Report]" height="79" width="369" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/07ca2318-c9e0-4b5d-bcba-95cec5cb4958.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Traditional search metrics still matter, but they answer different questions. Clicks and impressions in Google Search Console, and even website visits, don’t show whether answer engines mention or cite a brand, or how often that happens compared with competitors.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide lays out a repeatable process for benchmarking AEO using citation rate, share of voice, platform-level normalization, and executive-ready reporting. Together, those measures turn one-off prompt checks into a benchmark marketing teams can track and explain to leadership.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#why-seo-rankings-alone-do-not-benchmark-ai-search-performance"&gt;Why SEO Rankings Alone Do Not Benchmark AI Search Performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#which-benchmarks-matter-for-aeo-and-how-to-calculate-them"&gt;Which Benchmarks Matter for AEO and How to Calculate Them&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-i-benchmark-my-ai-search-performance-against-my-industry"&gt;How Do I Benchmark My AI Search Performance Against My Industry&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-i-normalize-results-across-answer-engines-and-prompts"&gt;How do I normalize results across answer engines and prompts?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-i-turn-benchmarks-into-an-improvement-plan"&gt;How do I turn benchmarks into an improvement plan?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-i-report-industry-benchmarks-to-leadership"&gt;How do I report industry benchmarks to leadership&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-ai-search-benchmarking"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About AI Search Benchmarking&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href="#turning-ai-search-benchmarks-into-a-program-not-a-one-time-project"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#turning-ai-search-benchmarks-into-a-program-not-a-one-time-project"&gt;Turning AI Search Benchmarks Into a Program, Not a One-Time Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why SEO Rankings Alone Do Not Benchmark AI Search Performance&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Ranking well in traditional search means a page appears on a search engine results page (SERP). A user can then click a result to visit the source.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot distinguishes &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/aeo-mentions-vs-citations"&gt;AEO mentions from citations&lt;/a&gt; this way: A mention names a brand in an AI-generated answer without a linked source, while a citation is an attributed source reference or linked URL. For this guide, a brand-level citation means an attributed source or linked URL from the brand’s domain.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Answer engine optimization measures a different layer of search visibility: &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/generative-engine-optimization"&gt;whether and how a brand or its content appears&lt;/a&gt; inside synthesized answers. AI-generated search features can also change click behavior. &lt;a href="https://ahrefs.com/blog/ai-overviews-reduce-clicks-update/"&gt;Ahrefs found&lt;/a&gt; that the presence of a &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-overviews"&gt;Google AI Overview&lt;/a&gt; correlated with a 58% lower average click-through rate for the top-ranking page in its December 2025 data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Traditional SEO metrics measure how pages perform in search results. AEO metrics measure whether brands and sources appear inside AI-generated answers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Featured resource: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/how-ai-is-impacting-seo"&gt;AI and SEO: What AI means for the future of SEO [Expert Tips &amp;amp; Interview]&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The following table shows common SEO metrics alongside AEO benchmarks. I cover the AEO benchmarks in more detail in the next section.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AEO benchmarking measures how often a brand appears or is cited across answer engines relative to a defined competitor set. Because generated answers can vary from run to run, these measures are estimates based on a defined set of prompts, platform, and collection window, not fixed rankings.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For Google AI Overviews specifically, &lt;a href="https://help.brightedge.com/resources/weekly-ai-search-insights/ai-overviews-one-year-presence-size-citing"&gt;BrightEdge’s analysis&lt;/a&gt; found that about 17% of cited sources also ranked in the organic top 10, meaning roughly five out of six citations came from outside page 1. BrightEdge reported 24% top-10 overlap in healthcare and 11% in finance. That does not make organic rankings irrelevant; it shows that organic ranking and AI Overview citation overlap can differ substantially by industry, so teams should measure both.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Which Benchmarks Matter for AEO and How to Calculate Them&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The four benchmarks below help measure and organize visibility in answer engines. They do not measure website or revenue impact on their own, so use them alongside traffic, conversion, and pipeline measures rather than treating them as replacements.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ran-ai-search-experiments"&gt;an experiment involving more than 500 queries across 20 platforms&lt;/a&gt;, Robert Carnes found that AI chatbots performed better on some direct-action prompts and could build arguments for opinion-based queries. At the same time, traditional search remained useful for specific and local information. The mixed result matters for benchmarking: Some AI interactions can satisfy a query without a click, but traditional search still plays an important role.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Separately, &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-aeo"&gt;HubSpot’s State of AEO 2026 report&lt;/a&gt; says 44% of surveyed marketers have made a business purchase based on brands they discovered through answer engines.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In a separate survey of more than 200 B2B decision-makers, 42% said an AI recommendation made a brand seem “more trustworthy — if AI recommends it, it’s probably vetted.” &lt;a href="https://marketingagainstthegrain.com/articles/new-research-on-how-b2b-decision-makers-user-ai-search"&gt;The research on B2B decision-makers and AI search&lt;/a&gt; found only 11% said an AI recommendation made a brand seem less trustworthy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/how-do-i-benchmark-my-ai-search-performance-against-my-industry-1-20261029-6335773.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="how do i benchmark AI seach performance against my industry, stats from HubSpot State of AEO"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;As Amanda Sellers, a former SEO and AEO strat...

&lt;p&gt;Most marketers use an AI assistant at work, but constantly switching between Claude, a CRM, and other apps breaks focus. That is where Claude integrations come in.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;/h1&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Connect HubSpot to Claude For Personalized Insights [Free Connector]" height="58" width="645" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Claude integrations link external tools and services directly to Claude, Anthropic’s AI assistant. The connectors allow Claude to read data and take action on behalf of a user without switching tabs or copying information between apps. Go-to-market (GTM) teams benefit from customer context that enriches responses with specific details rather than generic answers, while governance settings restrict connectors to read-only, approval-required, or blocked actions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/claude/connector"&gt;HubSpot Connector for Claude&lt;/a&gt; allows Claude to access HubSpot context, surface opportunities, and take action without switching tools. This article covers how to use Claude connectors, what data Claude can access through connectors, and a roundup of Claude integrations by GTM use case.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-claude-connectors-and-how-do-they-work"&gt;What are Claude connectors and how do they work?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-claude-connects-to-crm-data-securely"&gt;How Claude Connects to CRM Data Securely&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#best-claude-integrations-by-gtm-use-case"&gt;Best Claude Integrations by GTM Use Case&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-data-claude-can-access-through-connectors"&gt;What Data Claude Can Access Through Connectors&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-evaluate-a-claude-integration"&gt;How to Evaluate a&amp;nbsp;Claude Integration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#where-the-hubspot-connector-for-claude-fits"&gt;Where the HubSpot Connector For Claude Fits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-claude-integrations"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Claude Integrations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#doing-more-with-claude-integrations"&gt;Doing More With Claude Integrations&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are Claude connectors and how do they work?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude connectors bridge Claude and the tools that marketers, RevOps teams, and GTM leaders already use. Common examples include &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/sales/crm-integration"&gt;CRMs&lt;/a&gt;, project trackers, and calendars. When a connector is active, Claude can read data from those tools and take action inside them without the user leaving the Claude interface.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Developers build Claude connectors on the Model Context Protocol (MCP), a standard that lets Claude discover and call tools the way a browser calls an API. No code or endpoint configuration is required on the user’s side. Claude identifies available connectors, selects the right one for the task, and automatically passes the request through.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once a user connects an app, Claude can read from it, write to it, or both, depending on what that app exposes. The key design principle is that Claude inherits the user’s existing permissions. If a user can see a deal and engagement records in HubSpot, Claude can see them too. If a user cannot access a particular ticket queue in Zendesk, Claude cannot either. Claude integrations have no separate elevated-access or privilege-escalation path.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Every action Claude takes is logged and can be audited against the user’s account. The practical result is that users eliminate manual copy-pasting between tools.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For example, marketing teams don’t need to pull a call transcript from an app, open a CRM, draft an email, and then update the deal stage. Instead, team members can describe the outcome they want, and Claude handles the multi-step sequence using the context it has access to.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip:&lt;/strong&gt; For a comprehensive guide to using connectors to extend Claude’s capabilities, check out our &lt;a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11176164-use-connectors-to-extend-claude-s-capabilities."&gt;connector best practices&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How Claude Connects to CRM Data Securely&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Claude connectors securely connect to CRM &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/data-integration-strategy-and-tech"&gt;data&lt;/a&gt; through three distinct processes:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Permission inheritance.&lt;/strong&gt; When users connect a CRM like HubSpot to Claude, the connector uses per-user delegated OAuth. Claude integrations do not have their own login or a service account with broad access. The connectors operate through an existing session, inheriting exactly the permissions the user already has in that CRM. If a user cannot see a particular account or field due to pre-existing permission sets, field-level security, or sharing rules, Claude cannot either.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Org enablement.&lt;/strong&gt; Organizations on Enterprise plans can enable Claude connectors directly from Settings. As of August 2026, &lt;a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/15537633-authorize-mcp-connectors-for-your-entire-organization"&gt;Anthropic’s Enterprise-managed authorization&lt;/a&gt; allows admins to centrally provide connector access through the organization’s identity provider. Once admins enable connectors and map them to existing groups and roles, employees inherit the connection automatically on first login — no individual consent screens or per-user OAuth prompts required.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Action restrictions.&lt;/strong&gt; Beyond authentication, admins can control what Claude integrations do with the data. Per-tool permissions let users grant read-only access to one object while blocking writes to another. Admins can also disable specific tool calls from the same settings panel where connectors are enabled. Enterprise-managed auth supports an identity provider-only authentication requirement, which prevents employees from accidentally linking personal accounts to work-related CRM instances.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In addition to permission-based accessibility, organizational-level tool enabling, and task-specific restrictions, CRM contexts provide the specific data Claude needs to generate useful answers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For example, a sales rep can ask “what’s the last thing this specific account said before their renewal?” The rep will get correct answers only if Claude integrations can pull the relevant call notes, ticket history, and deal stage in one pass.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Without context, Claude either guesses or asks users to paste data manually. Manual data handling defeats the purpose of using connectors and creates &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/5-common-data-integration-challenges-and-how-to-solve-them"&gt;data integration problems&lt;/a&gt;. Claude’s security model makes CRM context available without compromising sensitive customer data. The same guardrails the CRM already enforces govern what Claude can see and do ...

&lt;p&gt;AI maturity explains why 98% of marketing teams now use AI in some way, yet only 10% report transformational results, according to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-ai"&gt;2026 State of AI in Marketing research&lt;/a&gt;. AI maturity measures how consistently a customer-facing team turns AI into measurable business outcomes, and it matters more than the number of tools or pilots you’ve launched.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;So if your team has tools, pilots, and plenty of enthusiasm but can't yet point to the revenue or customer experience gains, you're not alone. Adoption is mostly solved, but the gap is impact — and closing it starts with knowing where you stand.&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=b72f2b25-8cc9-4642-9a1b-1e675d3d273b&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Download Now: The State of AI in Marketing Report [Updated for 2026]" height="58" width="633" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/b72f2b25-8cc9-4642-9a1b-1e675d3d273b.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This guide defines the four AI maturity stages (Early, Emerging, Established, and Transformational), shows how to run an AI maturity assessment, and maps each stage to a next step with Loop Marketing. If you want the benchmarks first, &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-ai"&gt;download the 2026 State of AI in Marketing Report&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-is-ai-maturity-for-go-to-market-teams"&gt;What is AI maturity for go-to-market teams?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-the-ai-maturity-levels-in-marketing"&gt;What are the AI maturity levels in marketing?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-run-an-ai-maturity-assessment-and-benchmark"&gt;How to Run an AI Maturity Assessment and Benchmark&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#the-ai-maturity-index-for-gtm-teams"&gt;The AI Maturity Index For GTM Teams&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-move-up-the-ai-maturity-curve-with-loop-marketing"&gt;How to Move Up the AI Maturity Curve with Loop Marketing&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#data-readiness-and-responsible-ai-governance"&gt;Data Readiness and Responsible AI Governance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#activate-ai-across-the-funnel-and-measure-impact"&gt;Activate AI across the funnel and measure impact.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#your-next-moves-on-ai-maturity"&gt;Your Next Moves on AI Maturity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-ai-maturity"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions about AI Maturity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What is AI maturity for go-to-market teams?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI maturity measures how consistently a go-to-market team turns AI into measurable business outcomes. For marketing, that means AI runs in documented workflows, draws on clean customer data, operates under human oversight, and ties to metrics like MQLs, customer acquisition cost (CAC), and revenue. Sales and service use the same definition with different workflows and metrics.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Maturity beats counting pilots because pilots measure activity and maturity measures repeatability. A team can run ten experiments and still sit at the bottom of the curve if none connect to the CRM, have an owner, or show a before-and-after result.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketing leads to other GTM functions, with &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/state-of-generative-ai"&gt;42% of marketers reporting advanced AI use&lt;/a&gt; (Established or Transformational), compared with 27% in sales and 23% in service. For those functions, see the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/sales/sales-maturity-model"&gt;sales maturity model&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/service/customer-success-maturity-model"&gt;customer success maturity model&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;The Research Behind This Guide&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot’s 2026 State of AI in Marketing research:&lt;/strong&gt; 1,754 marketers across North America, Europe, Asia, Australia, and Latin America. Stages are respondent-rated, so they show how teams describe their own maturity, not an audit of results.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot’s cross-functional study:&lt;/strong&gt; 6,000+ professionals found that &lt;a href="https://offers.hubspot.com/state-of-ai"&gt;90% say their company uses AI and 6% rate it a “transformative” adopter&lt;/a&gt;. This is a different population than the marketing-only 98% and 10%, so don’t compare them directly.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;McKinsey’s 2026 State of AI survey:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.mckinsey.com/capabilities/quantumblack/our-insights/the-state-of-ai"&gt;1,719 participants in 97 countries&lt;/a&gt;, fielded May 4 to June 8, 2026, for an independent view of scaling and financial impact.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The four stages come from HubSpot’s research. The six-dimension scoring later in this guide is an editorial framework, not an official HubSpot metric. Treat all benchmarks as directional.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are the AI maturity levels in marketing?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;An AI maturity model includes stages that run from experimentation to scaled activation.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/blogbot/ai-maturity-2-20261026-2727881.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="AI maturity stages mapped to Loop Marketing"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The four AI maturity levels distinguish Early, Emerging, Established, and Transformational adoption patterns. A team can sit at different levels in different workflows, so score the workflow first.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early:&lt;/strong&gt; AI use is individual and ad hoc. No shared prompts, documented strategy, or CRM connection. Governance is informal. Results are anecdotal (“it saves me time”).&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emerging:&lt;/strong&gt; A few team-level use cases exist, each with an owner. Data access is partial, workflows run beside the core process, and measurement stops at time saved or output volume.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Established:&lt;/strong&gt; AI runs inside repeatable workflows across channels and uses connected customer data. A documented strategy and basic governance exist, agents handle defined multi-step tasks, and results are tracked against funnel metrics.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformational:&lt;/strong&gt; Workflows were redesigned around AI. Agents work under human oversight, governance runs daily, and results are measured against holdouts or phased tests. Saved time goes toward strategy.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The payoff at the top is measurable: &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/state-of-generative-ai"&gt;96% of Transformational adopters met or exceeded their MQL targets, and they were roughly 3.5x more likely to outperform CAC targets&lt;/a&gt;. Among all marketers surveyed, 72% said AI makes it easier to hit revenue and MQL targets, and about 65% said the same for CAC goals. These results are self-reported, so treat them as directional benchmarks.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;How These AI Maturity Levels Compare to Analyst Models&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Most AI maturity models agree that capability builds in stages. They differ in scope: the two best-known...

&lt;p&gt;Over the past few months, the HubSpot Blog team has been testing and comparing various AEO tools, including Scrunch vs. Semrush, and here’s the high-level takeaway if you’re trying to choose: Scrunch is a dedicated answer engine optimization (AEO) tool built to monitor how your brand shows up in AI answers, while Semrush folds AI visibility tracking into the SEO suite many teams already run.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Which tool is best for your team depends on your needs. This guide compares Scrunch vs. Semrush across four criteria that make a great AEO tool: answer engine coverage, citation tracking and auditability, reporting and export, and integration and workflow. Each comparison closes with a neutral verdict on who the tool serves best, and the guide ends with a validation plan you can run during free trials before you commit.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#why-aeo-matters-in-scrunch-vs-semrush"&gt;Why AEO Matters in Scrunch vs. Semrush&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-semrush-on-answer-engine-coverage"&gt;Scrunch vs. Semrush on Answer Engine Coverage&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-semrush-on-citation-tracking-and-auditability"&gt;Scrunch vs. Semrush on Citation Tracking and Auditability&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-semrush-on-reporting-and-export"&gt;Scrunch vs. Semrush on Reporting and Export&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#scrunch-vs-semrush-on-integration-and-workflows"&gt;Scrunch vs. Semrush on Integration and Workflows&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-to-validate-your-aeo-data-before-you-buy"&gt;How to Validate Your AEO Data Before You Buy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
